{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/969814-world-of-darkness-crossover-timeline","id":969814,"title":"World of Darkness crossover timeline","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-09-15T04:25:11-07:00","id":969814,"title":"World of Darkness crossover timeline","content":"I wanted to briefly discuss my personal fan project, the World of Darkness Crossover Timeline. In my headcanon, the classic World of Darkness and the Chronicles of Darkness exist as two separate but parallel universes. Although very few people are able to actually cross over from one universe to the other, a lot of people have counterparts in the other universe (witness the two Kindred named Maxwell who both become Prince of Chicago). Also, ideas cross over relatively freely between the two universes (note the similarities between the philosophy of the Lancea et Sanctum and the tenets of the Path of Night in the classic World of Darkness). My timeline postulates that the two timelines split at the time of the fall of Atlantis, which occurred around 11,000 BC, and have remained separate but interconnected ever since. What do you guys think?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My name is Colleen. My favorite song is &quot;Wildwood Flower.&quot; My ambition is to write the complete history of the White Wolf/Onyx Path universe.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11905-julianmoon","name":"JulianMoon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"253"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-15T06:07:27-07:00","id":969842,"title":"","content":"Well, the fall of Atlantis definitely didn't happen in 11000 BCE. Or at any point in history. It happened in a &quot;timeline&quot; that no longer ever existed. I'm also not clear on how that event happening or not happening would lead to WoD. However, I think the concept is cool, just quibbling over the point of divergence.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-15T06:57:46-07:00","id":969872,"title":"","content":"Charlaquin, I admit, I have not read Mage: the Awakening 2nd ed. However, from what I recall from first ed., the fall of Atlantis happened sometime in the very far distant past. It definitely happened after the creation of homo sapiens, because the inhabitants of Atlantis were human. Given those parameters, I find 11,000 BC to be a reasonable date for the Fall. Again, if I'm missing something specific, please correct me and I'll incorporate the new information into my timeline. As to why I chose it as the point of divergence, I wanted a great apocalypse to be the point at which the universes split. (Originally I used the end of the Primordial War, but then I decided I liked the Fall of Atlantis better.)<br /> <br /> On an unrelated point, I would love to chat sometime about some of the topics raised on the Transgender thread if you would be interested.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My name is Colleen. My favorite song is &quot;Wildwood Flower.&quot; My ambition is to write the complete history of the White Wolf/Onyx Path universe.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11905-julianmoon","name":"JulianMoon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"253"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-15T07:47:29-07:00","id":969899,"title":"","content":"It's actually been canon since I think Imperial Mysteries, and was even hinted at in the 1e Mage core. The 2e core is much more clear about it, though. Basically, when a Mage Ascends, history gets rewritten so that they no longer ever existed as a human/Mage. Once a supernal symbol, always a supernal symbol, and that applies retroactively as well. So, when the Mages of the great city (which was probably not actually called Atlantis, that's a name modern Mages applied to it) Ascended <i>en masse</i>, all the ensuing reality edits together completely erased the city from existence. So, for all the Diamond orders claim to be Atlantis reconstructionists, they have next to no idea what it was really like. It could have been in 11000 BCE. Or it could have been in 2015. It got retconned from reality, so in the current &quot;timeline&quot;, it never happened at all.<br /> <br /> I'd be happy to chat about trans stuff, feel free to PM me, or we can talk in the trans or LGBT thread.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-15T07:50:28-07:00","id":969902,"title":"","content":"Basically, you can't date the Fall of &quot;Atlantis&quot;, because &quot;Atlantis&quot; never happened, due to the actions of the former rulers of &quot;Atlantis&quot;... probably. And yes, logically that makes no sense, but that's what you get with timeline altering shenanigans.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-15T08:04:47-07:00","id":969914,"title":"","content":"I don't think it's a guarantee that the Atlanteans were human, either.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-15T08:20:28-07:00","id":969925,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/969814-world-of-darkness-crossover-timeline?p=969914#post969914\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think it's a guarantee that the Atlanteans were human, either.</div> </div> </div> </div>I rather like the idea of &quot;Atlanteans&quot; being Homo Neandertalis.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-15T08:31:24-07:00","id":969934,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/969814-world-of-darkness-crossover-timeline?p=969899#post969899\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Basically, when a Mage Ascends, history gets rewritten so that they no longer ever existed as a human/Mage.</div> </div> </div> </div>Point of clarification: When a mage Ascends they become part of the Supernal and thus the details of their existence tend to slide out of Sleepers' minds like any other facet of Awakened magic; the process of altering the Supernal on such a direct level in turn creates a ripple effect whose consequences may well extend into the past.<br /> <br /> A fairly solid theory for why a hypothetical historical Atlantis may have ceased to be is that the incident with the Celestial Ladder involved a whole lot of Atlantean mages Ascending at once and the resulting strain on existence derealized their homeland into myth.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-15T08:41:53-07:00","id":969941,"title":"","content":"I hate to do the whole linking up of two separate universes like this but Ascension did have an ascension concept. I suppose if JulianMoon wanted to they could have the Ascension of World of Darkness' mages erase a lot of key aspects of that game, offering a clean slate free of the Triat and Abrahamic God where the Chronicles could 'evolve' as it did.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-15T08:45:32-07:00","id":969944,"title":"","content":"It's been years since I read Mage: the Awakening. Please tell me how much of the following is canon and how much is my headcanon: a group of mages known as the Exarchs seized control of Atlantis and built a device called the Celestial Ladder to physically breach the Supernal Realms. The Celestial Ladder exploded, destroying Atlantis. This is my understanding of how the Fall of Atlantis happened. The Fall was the result of hubris on the part of the Exarchs, completely the opposite of the mass Ascension/enlightenment scenario Charlaquin describes. I may end up keeping part or all of my version anyway, but I would like to know what canon really says before I go ahead and change it. Thanks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My name is Colleen. My favorite song is &quot;Wildwood Flower.&quot; My ambition is to write the complete history of the White Wolf/Onyx Path universe.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11905-julianmoon","name":"JulianMoon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"253"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-15T09:08:23-07:00","id":969969,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JulianMoon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/969814-world-of-darkness-crossover-timeline?p=969944#post969944\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's been years since I read Mage: the Awakening. Please tell me how much of the following is canon and how much is my headcanon: a group of mages known as the Exarchs seized control of Atlantis and built a device called the Celestial Ladder to physically breach the Supernal Realms. The Celestial Ladder exploded, destroying Atlantis. This is my understanding of how the Fall of Atlantis happened.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's canonically the story that the Diamond orders and the Seers of the Throne have constructed to explain what may have happened during the fall. You could say it's the Mage characters' head canon. But there's no way of knowing what actually happened, in part because it didn't actually ever happen in the post-Fall version of history.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JulianMoon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/969814-world-of-darkness-crossover-timeline?p=969944#post969944\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Fall was the result of hubris on the part of the Exarchs, completely the opposite of the mass Ascension/enlightenment scenario Charlaquin describes. I may end up keeping part or all of my version anyway, but I would like to know what canon really says before I go ahead and change it. Thanks.</div> </div> </div> </div>Err... It was totally the result of the Hubris of the Mages of the great city that caused the Fall. The Celestial Ladder was (according to the story Mages tell themselves) what allowed them to Ascend, and their Ascension is what retconned the Time Before out of existence. Ascending is an inherently Hubristic act.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-15T09:09:28-07:00","id":969970,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/969814-world-of-darkness-crossover-timeline?p=969941#post969941\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I hate to do the whole linking up of two separate universes like this but Ascension did have an ascension concept. I suppose if JulianMoon wanted to they could have the Ascension of World of Darkness' mages erase a lot of key aspects of that game, offering a clean slate free of the Triat and Abrahamic God where the Chronicles could 'evolve' as it did.</div> </div> </div> </div>Unless bits of the Weaver remained, and began to rebuild Itself with whatever tools were handy, to establish the Infrastructure for Its restoration...<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-15T09:34:07-07:00","id":969987,"title":"","content":"So, are we proposing that the World of Darkness <i>was</i> the Time Before, and the Fall was the Apocalypse/Gehenna/whatever the other supers called it? The Exarchs were group of MtAs Mages who Ascended during the end times and created a new universe under their (relatively hermetic) Paradigm? It's a little Mage-centric for my taste, but it could work.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-15T09:55:13-07:00","id":970001,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/969814-world-of-darkness-crossover-timeline?p=969987#post969987\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, are we proposing that the World of Darkness <i>was</i> the Time Before, and the Fall was the Apocalypse/Gehenna/whatever the other supers called it? The Exarchs were group of MtAs Mages who Ascended during the end times and created a new universe under their (relatively hermetic) Paradigm? It's a little Mage-centric for my taste, but it could work.</div> </div> </div> </div>Again there's no reason the Exarchs were human. They might have been tyrannical mages, or vampires, or some sort of ephemeral entities.<br /> <br /> But it wasn't really about Apocalypse or Gehenna as much as the Mage's Ascension. Just a glimpse at my 20th edition does confirm the whole mass ascension thing. Specifically, 'Because of that particular paradox, many mages reach for a lesser goal instead: they want to make the world Ascend. And they'll tell you that's the ultimate benevolence. And they'll be lying then, because it's not. Although you might disagree with this opinion, as many mages do, in my mind such universal Ascension is the ultimate form of slavery. It replaces individual revelation with communal unity, getting all sleepers to awaken the way we think they should. It's a utopian goal, with the same flaw as all Utopias: the insistence that everyone conform to someone else's ideas.' This could fit in with the entire community of mages Ascending, with a little bit of tyranny added in as well.<br /> <br /> Perhaps it was flawed, or they were flawed, or flaws crept in from the outside. It is Mage-centric, especially as it involves the elimination of every other supernatural group, but we do have a common link in Voormas. And people thinking the world revolves around Mage is not exactly new.<br /> <br /> Now all that said, I don't believe it one bit. I have my own theories for the Chronicles. But JulianMoon wasn't asking for those. They want the world to exist as two separate but parallel universes, and if the World of Darkness had a mirror and one dealt with Ascension and another didn't, or ascension allows for the creation of a new world, you could have both worlds parallel with a few leaps.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 09-15-2016, 12:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-15T10:20:43-07:00","id":970016,"title":"","content":"I thought there were multiple &quot;Alantises&quot; that got erased at least partially from the time line by Ascensions, battles between ascended beings, ect...<br /> <br /> Also weird though, but could Pangaeans Ascend?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-15T10:33:09-07:00","id":970021,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/969814-world-of-darkness-crossover-timeline?p=970016#post970016\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I thought there were multiple &quot;Alantises&quot; that got erased at least partially from the time line by Ascensions, battles between ascended beings, ect...</div> </div> </div> </div>The various Ruins of the Time Before don't all match each other, giving rise to the idea that there have been more than one Time Befores.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"htt